WEBVTT

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.370
<b>Chio's</b>

00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:21.370
School Road

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.820
<b>Smoke on the Sailor</b>

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.170
Hey, you have some kind of situation you'd 
like to encounter before you die, right?

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:39.740
Uh, like what?

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.720
Well... like having some hot foreign 
guy ask me for directions,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.420
then we try to communicate with gestures,

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:49.770
and things start to heat up, 
and just like that...

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.290
Just like what?!

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.560
Do you have anything you want 
to do before you die, Chio-chan?

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.380
Oh, I do!

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.510
You know how people throw 
cigarettes out of cars?

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.850
I want to pick one up in a cool way and say...

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.270
You dropped something.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.520
And flick it back into the car!

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:12.600
Th-That's it?

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:14.860
Why not? Isn't that super cool?

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:20.390
Actually, it seems like you 
could do that pretty regularly.

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.260
Like with that lady.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.100
Hmm, I'm not sure...

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.130
Looks like she got a phone call.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.750
Hey, it's me.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:32.720
Yeah, could you do something 
about that part-timer?

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:33.750
Chio-chan!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.930
<i>Sh-She caught it directly?!</i>

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.910
Ow!

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:50.600
I leaped too far! Ow, my clavicle!

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:53.520
She's leaving!

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:55.940
W-Wait!

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:57.990
No, you wait!

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.860
Goodness, young lady.

00:03:01.190 --> 00:03:03.220
Looks like you took quite the tumble.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.530
Sorry about my friend! 
She's a bit clumsy!

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:13.630
Nanoha
Bank

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.800
Hey, are you okay?

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.630
Man, I always forget how 
passionate you can get.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:17.050
Wait, did you actually get hurt?

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:21.760
Manana... I lost my chance 
to throw this away.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.430
Hurry up and get rid of that thing!

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:29.300
Well, I mean... It's not lit anymore...

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.470
So it's just trash, right?

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.860
Maybe I won't get in trouble for 
having it, as long as I don't smoke it...

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.790
<i>I can just tell...</i>

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:45.030
<i>Chio-chan's the type to think 
that smoking looks cool.</i>

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:46.990
<i>Come to think of it, that one time...</i>

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.680
Characters who smoke are good characters.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.750
Oh, I see.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:58.270
Chio-chan, that's just a 
cigarette that's been put out.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.210
What you're actually doing 
is just picking up litter...

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.900
So it's legal!

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:14.600
Good! Good! Look right over here! Smile!

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:16.750
L-Like this?

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:17.920
Yes! Perfect!

00:04:17.920 --> 00:04:19.720
Don't let the cigarette touch your mouth,

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.530
because that'll mean all kinds of trouble!

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.700
Good! Good! Perfectly legal!

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:25.660
And legal.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.030
Also legal.

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:29.280
Yes, legal!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:32.540
This girl is so bad!

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.440
<i>This is amazing... It's like I'm not even me.</i>

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.900
<i>I feel like a bad girl.</i>

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.600
Chio-chan! Let's take more! More!

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.210
I'm getting into it now!

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.720
Chio-chan, you're amazing! 
Look right over here!

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.640
<i>I can't believe she's letting me take so many 
photos that would blow up if they got out!</i>

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:53.270
<i>I can't stop drooling!</i>

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:55.560
<i>I want to put these online so bad!</i>

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.530
Look more like an assassin! 
Yes! More! More!

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.960
Give me that murder face! Murder face!

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.080
Let's try walking a little.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.410
Imagine you're the bad guy making his 
first appearance in a battle manga.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:23.260
Look at this miraculous shot!

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.530
Oh, my gosh... I've never 
seen anything like this...

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.680
Y-You should try, Manana.

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.770
No, I'm good...

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.600
Do it, Manana!

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.720
<i>What the hell is she saying?</i>

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.340
<i>There's no way I'd let her take 
such risky photos of me!</i>

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.860
<i>I've gotta calm her down...</i>

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.100
Hey, boy...

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:53.540
The cat! It totally ruined the picture!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.950
You're trying to look so hot, 
but you look so dumb!

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:58.660
Look at this miraculous shot!

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.310
Hey, the cat's leaving!

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.780
Hey, take one now! Take one now!

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:03.840
Come on!

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.140
Yay!

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.080
Man, that was so much fun.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:14.300
Crap... I didn't think I'd end up 
getting mine taken, too...

00:06:14.300 --> 00:06:16.350
You looked great, too, Manana.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.360
You were actually sorta... sexy.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:25.110
Wanna do another shoot in my room tonight?

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.200
Okay, I'll hold on to this.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.740
You're just going to keep 
hiding it in your hand?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:33.760
It's more fragile than I thought...

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.830
So when I get to school, I'll wrap it up 
in something and keep it in my bag.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:37.830
I see.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.300
<i>This is truly...</i>

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.610
<i>A mission to bring in a hazardous substance.</i>

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.610
<i>We're going to protect this "toy" 
until we get out of school.</i>

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:51.070
<i>A day-long mission is about to begi—</i>

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.220
Something stinks.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.670
Wait... but I... took a bath this morning...

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:59.140
This stench is unbearable.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.980
All of you, stop where you are! 
I smell tobacco!

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.820
You may be able to fool your parents, 
but you can't fool my nose.

00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:14.740
<i>What? No way. Can he actually 
smell this one used cigarette?</i>

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:18.780
There's no doubt about it. 
The smell's getting stronger.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.050
You... No, it's not you.

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:23.330
I-It's not me!

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:26.230
<i>I had let my guard down...</i>

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:31.330
<i>Bringing a used cigarette 
to school was insane!</i>

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:35.640
<i>It was basically like playing 
with an unexploded bomb!</i>

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:39.060
<i>If he finds this cigarette, 
it's going to be a huge deal.</i>

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:42.480
<i>Worst case scenario, we might get expelled!</i>

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:46.790
<i>Oh, shit! If he looks at our cell phones...</i>

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:49.030
<i>Those photos...</i>

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.330
It's you.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:03.120
<i>I'm finished.</i>

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:06.540
Yes... It's me.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.820
Where did you get this?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:15.140
S-Someone threw it out the 
window, so I picked it up.

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:19.960
Oh?

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:25.200
Well done. I'll make sure to get rid of this.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:26.270
Huh?

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:27.750
U-Um...

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.750
Chio-chan?!

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.570
You don't think there's a 
possibility that I smoked it?

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:35.490
Uh, not really.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.060
It's faint, but there's lipstick on the end,

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.410
and this brand is pretty strong.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:45.330
It wouldn't suit a child. 
I can't imagine you smoking this, Miyamo.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:49.910
<i>I... I feel like he might 
actually be insulting me...</i>

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.550
B-B-But just maybe I did smoke it!

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:59.240
I'm... I'm a pretty bad girl, you know.

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.140
Huh?

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.210
A bad girl? Seriously?

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.000
What's that pose supposed to be? A gun?

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:13.690
Well, there's your answer.

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:17.440
I'm going to show you those photos, then!

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:17.440
No! Don't!

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.390
Don't stop me, Manana!

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:21.370
Chio-chan! You're going 
to drag me down with you!

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.370
<b>Chio's</b>

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.370
School Road

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.980
<i>Chio's School Road</i>.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:26.990
Hey, Gotou-chan, what's that?

00:09:26.990 --> 00:09:30.250
Oh, a first-year picked up some litter.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.400
I hate cigarettes.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.170
Only idiots smoke, right?

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:37.740
Is that so? This brand is 
actually quite historic.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:41.090
People like Akutagawa Ryuunosuke 
and Dazai Osamu smoked it.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:42.600
Really?

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:47.020
Listen up. Even if it involves smoking, 
you should never be prejudiced.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.140
Okay!

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:51.320
<i>But I'm pretty sure a minor 
shouldn't agree with that...</i>

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:56.860
Preliminary Career Survey
This year, we will be doing a preliminary career survey with all the students.
We believe that this will be especially useful for 3rd-years when they decide what path
they're going to take. Please try to fill in all 3 choices.
Choosing Career/School
Career | School
Choice 1 | Choice 1
Choice 2 | Choice 2

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:57.660
<b>Taking the Cherry Blossom in Your Hand</b>

00:09:53.390 --> 00:09:55.410
Man, are they really asking first-years

00:09:55.410 --> 00:09:56.860
about their career paths?

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:59.450
What are you going to do, Manana?

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.840
I wrote that I'm going to be a teacher.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.720
What? I've never heard you 
mention that before.

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:05.700
It's just a dummy answer.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.650
Telling the teachers that you 
plan to be a teacher yourself

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:10.880
should go over pretty well, right?

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.640
Yeah, I guess... 
Wait, what are you trying to do?

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:16.360
Get brownie points.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.590
You're scum, you know that?

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:23.000
I mean, wouldn't it be way better 
if we didn't have to get a job?

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:27.620
I wouldn't say... I mean, I think 
work could be fun in some ways.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:29.610
All right. Why don't we make a bet?

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:30.290
Huh?

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:33.280
We're going to ask the first adult we see,

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.480
"Do you think your job is fun?"

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.300
And we'll bet 100 yen on their answer.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:39.800
If they say it's fun, you win.

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.050
What? We're really going 
to ask strangers that?

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:42.570
Yup!

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:43.790
<i>Wait...</i>

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:46.120
<i>Knowing Manana, she might actually—</i>

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:49.040
Shit. I want to quit my job so bad.

00:10:50.010 --> 00:10:50.960
This sucks.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.160
Smirk.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:54.040
What? No way!

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.130
Sir, are you okay?

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:58.200
<i>Whoa! She actually did it!</i>

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.080
Are you having problems at work?

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.470
Uh, no, I...

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:03.290
I saw you and got a bit worried...

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:06.640
Well, I tried to live my life acting cool...

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.660
But now that I've joined adult society,

00:11:08.660 --> 00:11:12.520
I realized that I can't even 
deliver newspapers properly...

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.070
<i>That bike... Oh, I guess it belongs 
to that newspaper delivery guy.</i>

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:16.440
Shibasei Newspaper

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.550
<i>Wait a sec, that's—</i>

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:19.510
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.360
<i>Andou-san from the motorcycle gang!</i>

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:26.940
I keep getting all these complaints... 
I'm so going to get yelled at later.

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:28.290
Shh...

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:36.170
So you're saying work is not fun, right?

00:11:38.650 --> 00:11:43.140
Well, it's rough at times, 
but it's definitely worth doing...

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:44.550
<i>Huh?</i>

00:11:44.900 --> 00:11:47.060
I'm not sure about fun,

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:52.970
but I just personally don't 
think this job is for me.

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:55.150
<i>He's trying to act cool all of a sudden?</i>

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:59.600
Honestly, it's a pain. I think I'll just set 
the rest of the papers on fire and quit.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:01.700
No!

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.680
You finally started working!

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:08.490
Sulking and quitting isn't cool at all!

00:12:09.140 --> 00:12:10.540
B-Bloody Bu—

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:14.060
We'll help you out, so let's go!

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.580
We have a little time to spare,

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:21.750
so let's finish up the rest 
of this delivery, okay?

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.940
O-Okay.

00:12:25.940 --> 00:12:28.560
This is all I have left... Help me out!

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:30.930
Come on, Manana!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:31.930
What?!

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:33.840
The first place is down here!

00:12:32.790 --> 00:12:34.790
Wait for me!

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:34.790
What about your bike?

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:37.270
It's fine. These are my last papers.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:41.030
I'll have you two deliver to the house with 
the red roof and the one across from it.

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:41.940
Okay.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.360
I'll go take care of all the 
deliveries on the other side.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:45.330
Bloody—

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.740
It's Miyamo. This is Nonomura.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:48.910
Hi...

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:50.790
Th-The name's Andou...

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.880
I didn't think we were actually 
going to help deliver newspapers.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.630
Think of it as helping someone out. Besides...

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.400
you might find some joy in working.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:09.180
It's already late, so why don't we ring 
the doorbell and hand it to them directly?

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:12.020
<b>Ookawara
Stationery</b>

00:13:09.610 --> 00:13:11.510
Why do I have to do this?

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.350
Sakaguchi

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:24.380
Um... I'm sorry we're late. 
H-Here's your paper.

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.610
<b>Shibasei Newspaper</b>

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.610
<b>10,000 tuna wash up on Kasugai Beach</b>

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:26.610
<b>Locals Ecstatic</b>

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.490
I already saw that on TV!

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.140
Okay, I'll do the next one...

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.350
<b>Tanaka</b>

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:03.310
Um, here's your paper.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.320
I know it's a little late...

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.270
I'm really sorr—

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:12.330
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.740
U-Uh, hey!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:16.540
Wait, it's not bleeding, is it? Ow!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.880
I'm never doing that again. 
I'm never going to work.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:25.260
Never working again...

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:28.800
Wha— I see. You handed 
them the papers directly...

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:30.680
I should've told you!

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:35.430
Those born in the Showa era get 
really pissed if their paper is late.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.970
What? Why? It's just a newspaper...

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:41.550
The Showa era didn't have the 
pressure-free education system.

00:14:41.550 --> 00:14:44.870
What they went through was the 
loathsome cramming education.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:45.730
Hurgh!

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:48.780
So if they don't see those lines of 
printed words to start their day,

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:51.410
they lose themselves and become violent!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.710
<i>Th-They've got no chill...</i>

00:14:54.710 --> 00:14:57.470
<i>Those poor people born in the Showa era.</i>

00:14:58.080 --> 00:15:00.870
Isn't the problem that you're so late?

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.340
Why were you so late to begin with?

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:08.530
Er, um, uh...

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:12.590
It seems there've been some early morning 
incidents resulting in injury lately.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.950
I kept getting questioned 
by all these policemen.

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:15.480
Excuse me, do you have a moment?

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:16.580
What is it?

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.520
I got annoyed and raised 
my voice a little, and...

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.640
I told you! I have nothing to do with it!

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:22.700
Hey, yelling makes you even more suspicious.

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:23.830
I require backup!

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.520
I just ended up further delayed...

00:15:28.850 --> 00:15:30.360
Andou-san...

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.030
Considering how you look, it's—

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:35.210
It's okay! This isn't your 
fault at all, Andou-san.

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:36.700
Stuff like this happens!

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:37.950
Miyamo...

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:42.290
Please don't get upset. It doesn't suit you.

00:15:42.290 --> 00:15:44.880
Let's keep our heads up! All the time!

00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:46.830
I see... Keep my head up.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.300
Yup!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:51.090
<i>There's something off 
about Chio-chan's intensity...</i>

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.640
<i>I-It can't be!</i>

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:56.620
Where to next?

00:15:56.620 --> 00:15:58.560
It's just around the corner...

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:00.480
Hang on a sec!

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:04.460
Damn it. He is out there.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.360
The annoying customer you mentioned...

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:08.530
Is that him?

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:12.370
Yeah. If I'm even a little late, he waits 
in front of his apartment like that forever,

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:14.130
lecturing on and on.

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:15.660
Man, the paper's late.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:17.370
He's not getting away with this.

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:20.790
I'm hours behind today...

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.890
This is going to suck, 
but I don't have a choice...

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:23.960
Definitely not forgiving him!

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:23.960
I'll go get yelled at.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:25.020
Wait!

00:16:25.840 --> 00:16:30.550
When you deliver papers, you just have to 
get the paper into the mail slot, right?

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.150
Manana.

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:33.690
Yeah, I get it.

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:35.300
What are you planning to do?

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.720
We're gonna keep our heads held high!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:38.010
The stairs are on the other side!

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:49.570
Damn it... I'm gonna lecture
him until he pisses himself.

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:52.010
What's wrong with kids these days?

00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:53.860
They don't take us adults seriously!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:58.330
I need to teach them how rough the world is.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.200
Seriously, why do I—

00:17:02.350 --> 00:17:05.670
Damn it. He's still not here? 
That young punk...

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:11.920
Damn it, he's late.

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:25.610
You okay?

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.320
Huh? The paper's right here.

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.760
You're amazing, Miyamo!

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.900
I know, right?!

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:43.220
When you use a dagger, 
you don't rely on arm strength...

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:46.250
You hold it by your abdomen and stab 
with all of your body weight!

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.960
Yay! We finished all the deliveries!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.250
Collective mailboxes are the best!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:54.060
Man, thank goodness!

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:56.340
Okay...

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.860
Hey, Miyamo.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:17:58.860
Whoa, you're close!

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:00.610
Huh? Are there still more?

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:02.680
Uh, no, that's not it...

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:09.930
Hey, listen...

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:14.530
I, uh... B-Because of you... 
Because of you...

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:20.050
Because of you, I decided I'd 
keep this job a little longer.

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:27.440
I see. It's a bit rough, 
but it is a fun job, isn't it?

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:29.020
Yeah.

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.940
Chio-chan. We're about out of time.

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:38.260
Look, we're gonna be late.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.030
Well, good luck, Andou-san.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:41.050
Th-Thanks...

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:49.900
Hey...

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:52.290
Chio-chan, that guy—

00:18:52.290 --> 00:18:53.230
Manana.

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:55.870
Wh-What?

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:00.570
So... give me 100 yen.

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:01.340
Huh?

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:03.550
Hey, we made a bet.

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:05.490
We're going to ask the first adult we see,

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:07.630
Before we left, I asked him if delivering 
papers was fun, and he said yes,

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.630
"Do you think your job is fun?"

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:08.880
so I win.

00:19:07.630 --> 00:19:09.500
And we'll bet 100 yen on their answer.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:12.420
<i>Don't tell me she...</i>

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:14.340
Come on, now. Come on.

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.900
<i>The way she was acting and 
the stuff she was saying...</i>

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:18.890
<i>It wasn't actually romantic,</i>

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:23.930
<i>but she made him say that 
because she wanted 100 yen...</i>

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:28.020
<i>She's so... so...</i>

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:30.940
Come on! Hurry up! 100 yen, please!

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.940
<b>Chio's</b>

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.940
School Road

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:33.660
<i>Chio's School Road</i>.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.790
So her name's Miyamo...

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:40.860
She's always helping me out...

00:19:41.100 --> 00:19:43.780
What a great girl!

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:47.680
<i>What the hell is that face? 
She pisses me off so much.</i>

00:19:46.660 --> 00:19:49.040
100 yen!

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.040
<b>Manana's</b>

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.040
School Road

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.600
Manana's School Road.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.520
You said you became friends with Hosokawa-san

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:57.160
after you dove head-first into some garbage,

00:19:57.160 --> 00:19:58.880
but what does that even mean?

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:02.130
Oh... Yeah, that...

00:20:03.150 --> 00:20:07.500
I see. You caused a huge 
fuss to try to fool her.

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.950
You always have to overdo everything.

00:20:11.530 --> 00:20:13.310
Then what would you have done?

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.770
A single expression would've 
been more than enough!

00:20:16.010 --> 00:20:17.180
Like what?!

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:20.070
It's...

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:23.490
the expression when you look like you aren't 
greeting someone, but you actually are!

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:27.410
The expression when you look like you aren't 
greeting someone, but you actually are?!

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:32.330
First of all, the one doing the greeting 
isn't even paying attention to nearby randos.

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:36.180
Which means, when you're not sure, 
if you greet them with a vague expression,

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:37.950
you wouldn't be ignoring them,

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:41.260
and if they weren't greeting you, 
you can just walk by without being noticed.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:44.300
It's not anything people around you 
would notice, so the risk is low.

00:20:44.830 --> 00:20:48.180
I see... So what kind of expression is that?

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:49.080
It's...

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:50.350
Morning!

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:53.270
<i>One of the popular girls from Manana's class?</i>

00:20:53.570 --> 00:20:56.920
<i>Hey, this is the same situation 
I was in the other day.</i>

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:59.690
<i>She may or may not be greeting Manana...</i>

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:02.610
<i>What are you going to do, Manana?!</i>

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:04.570
Hey...

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.910
I-It's perfect!

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:12.870
<i>She's expressing surprise, hesitation, 
and joy with her eyes and eyebrows...</i>

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:15.580
<i>And her lips may or may not 
be giving a greeting...</i>

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:18.300
<i>Th-This is...</i>

00:21:18.300 --> 00:21:21.120
<i>The expression when you look like you aren't 
greeting someone, but you actually are!</i>

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:23.890
Nonomura-san!

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:26.220
<i>Whoa! The greeting actually wor—</i>

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:27.780
Are you feeling sick?

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:32.640
<i>Uh-oh... She just thinks 
Manana's acting weird now.</i>

00:21:36.050 --> 00:21:39.030
Yes... My stomach doesn't feel g— Augh!

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.320
Nonomura-san?

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:41.080
What's wrong?

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.280
Is she okay?

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.190
<i>Whoa, people are gathering.</i>

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:45.480
Nonomura-san!

00:21:45.480 --> 00:21:48.120
It's okay... This happens all 
the time. It'll pass soon...

00:21:48.120 --> 00:21:48.790
Are you okay?

00:21:48.790 --> 00:21:49.770
Should I call an ambulance?

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:51.320
An ambulance?! No, that's okay...

00:21:51.320 --> 00:21:52.850
Oh, I think it's getting better...

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.040
No, really!

00:21:54.040 --> 00:21:54.730
It's okay.

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:56.380
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:21:56.380 --> 00:21:57.960
<i>I'm gonna run!</i>

00:23:27.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:30.430
Next time on <i>Chio's School Road</i>,

00:23:30.430 --> 00:23:33.220
"Thank You, George" and "Mananacchio."

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:34.370
Look forward to it!

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:36.020
100 yen!

00:23:39.030 --> 00:23:39.980
This is too long!
